e person made was it  singular plural was it you know tens and  so forth by far the biggest problem was  word usage people don't have a  sufficient sense of what a word what  words mean and which words they are used  with together with in combination with  and so and so you know for example very  common for people to say I am very  interesting in movies instead of  interested now you can get in to all  kinds of terms of Gerrans and  participles or whatever it's not gonna  help that person has to and and I'll get  into what I do but they have to get used  to the ideas I'm interested in that's a  phrase I'm interested in music I'm  interested in art I'm interested in  literature I'm excited about the game  tomorrow I'm not exciting about the game  and there are many many more examples  like that you know so many people  particularly Chinese people Japanese  people even I go even I go you know even  I work hard work hard I want to see even  if even though ok throwing a grammatical  tournament that is not gonna help people  have to focus on it that's why I say in  my own case say Slavik case endings I  just have to save the phrases say in  link focus on those phrases here's how  it you know very often the preposition  will determine the case or certain verbs  determine the case and so I have to  highlight those if I'm reading in a book  I underline them if I'm listening I  listen for it and slowly with enough  with enough exposure to the language  through listening and reading and I  might add  you know I eventually have to speak and  you have to use the words I often say  when I'm starting in a language I do a  lot of listening and reading to build up  my vocabulary and I'm approaching 3,000  words in Arabic so I'll soon have to  start speaking ugh but not argh I'm  looking forward to it  but you have to start using it and  making mistakes and get the mistakes  corrected and you'll make the mistake  again and slowly the brain gets used to  the structure the usage in the language  and all of our brains are capable of  learning and acquiring the language in  this way not all of us can understand  the grammatical terms the grammatical  explanation is not all of us want to do  the drills but if we expose ourselves to  enough of the content and if we want to  improve you know and very often no first  of all let me say so when I start  speaking with the tutor  at link I get back a report with 1015  phrases where I made a mistake so I then  import these a nice study these phrases  and very likely the next three or four  times at least from my own experience  that I speak with a tutor I will make  the same mistake again and I'll get it  corrected again but over time gradually  I'll start you know improving with  regard to these structures but I also  notice other structures if I'm attentive  to the language if I'm doing enough  listening and reading and so gradually  gradually my usage my word usage my you  know accuracy in terms of using the  structures of the language will improve  and so rather than relying on  grammatical terms and grammatical  explanations the issue is here's how we  say this in say English which is my  language or whatever your language  happens to be this is how we say this in  my language here's how they say it in  the language that I am learning so this  structure or this phrase equals this  phrase and so gradually as you're  listening to content and reading and  making meaning of it and and starting to  rely on the structures of the language  you are learning  the brain is slowly getting used to it  and so I think with regard to grammar  errors in fact there's all kinds of  research that shows that correcting  doesn't change things I have some  difficulty with this because corrections  is one of the ways in which you start to  notice what's happening in the language  it doesn't correct you overnight and you  need to be corrected many many times but  it's part of what helps you notice  massive exposure helps you